  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nA mid-level high centered over New Mexico will maintain hot and \nmostly dry conditions through the weekend. Afternoon highs will \ngenerally range from the mid 90s near the coast to around 105 \ndegrees across the western Brush Country, with heat index values \ncommonly between 105 and 112 degrees, increasing towards 115 later \nin the week. Prompting a Heat Advisory for Tuesday afternoon/evening \nwith more advisories likely to follow this week. HeatRisk will \nremain moderate to major across much of South Texas, with localized \nextreme values possible where the hottest temperatures persist.\n\nA subtle pattern change is possible early next week as a mid-level \ntrough extends southwestward from northeast of our region toward the \nVictoria Crossroads, along the eastern periphery of the ridge. This \nmay provide enough lift and moisture for isolated showers and \nthunderstorms, with rain chances currently around 15-20%. Otherwise, \nno significant change in temperatures is expected.",
